  "user_request_original": "Optimize a 20-layer planar stack on Al substrate with air incidence. Layer sequence: Cr | HfO2 | SiO2 | HfO2 | SiO2 | HfO2 | SiO2 | HfO2 | SiO2 | HfO2 | SiO2 | HfO2 | SiO2 | HfO2 | SiO2 | HfO2 | SiO2 | HfO2 | SiO2 | HfO2. Initialize from iteration_24 best candidate thicknesses [1.0, 123.0, 94.0, 4.0, 22.0, 52.0, 139.0, 83.0, 40.0, 98.0, 231.0, 43.0, 4.0, 123.0, 48.0, 113.0, 155.0, 14.0, 70.0, 154.0] nm. Set Cr layer (index 0) thickness bounds to [0.5, 6.0] nm. Set all dielectric layers (indices 1-19) bounds to [1.0, 300.0] nm. Use gradient_thickness optimizer. Initialize 70% of candidates from baseline with small perturbations; initialize remaining 30% with random thickness draws uniformly distributed in [baseline - 50 nm, baseline + 50 nm] for each layer. Evaluate at normal incidence, unpolarized. Spectral objectives: maximize absorptance in 400-700 nm band, maximize reflectance in 700-2000 nm band. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 400-700 nm, 700-2000 nm. soft objectives: high absorptance in 400-700 nm; low reflectance in 400-700 nm; high reflectance in 700-2000 nm. behaviors to suppress or avoid: high reflectance in 400-700 nm; high absorptance in 700-2000 nm. manufacturing constraints: total layer count not exceeding 20.",
